{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>A great treasure</b> — gathered, but plundered is turmoil in the treasure. Its meaning: <b>trouble</b> [is] from <b>וַיָּהָם יְהֹוָה</b> [\"and YHWH threw into turmoil\"] (Genesis 11:7), meaning that the wicked man storms at people: a great turmoil [is] their wealth."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:59.986316733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}